{
  "_note": "swarf material palette. STUDENT-SAFE STARTING VALUES, not optimal ones — every entry is slow, shallow and survivable, and every one of them can be pushed once you know what the cut sounds like. Feeds and speeds assume HSS tooling, which is the limiting factor: HSS runs at roughly a third the cutting speed of the coated carbide in Langmuir's MR-1 chart, so RPM here drops as the tool gets bigger rather than sitting at 8000. Machine limits: 8000 rpm, 2540 mm/min.",
  "_tooling": "HSS, 2-flute for everything except mild steel, which assumes 4-flute. RPM comes from a conservative cutting speed (aluminum 60, brass 45, mild steel 20 m/min) as rpm = Vc x 1000 / (pi x diameter), capped at the machine's 8000. Feed comes from chip load: feed = rpm x flutes x fz, fz at the low end. The tool library has no flute-count field, so nothing adapts automatically — running a 4-flute where 2 is assumed halves the chip load (safe, though it can rub in aluminum); running a 2-flute where 4 is assumed doubles it. With carbide instead of HSS, every RPM here can roughly triple: see _source.",
  "_units": "feed mm/min · plunge mm/min · spindle rpm · stepdown mm · stepover fraction of tool diameter · ramp angle degrees",
  "_tools": "by_tool keyed to endmill diameter in mm, matching the endmills in the default tool library: 1.5875 = 1/16 inch, 3.175 = 1/8 inch, 6.35 = 1/4 inch. The closest diameter wins for any other tool. 1/8 and 1/4 are the shop's working sizes.",
  "_ramp": "ramp.angle drives camEaseAngle, ramp.ease drives camEaseDown — the tool walks down into the cut instead of drilling in on a flute that may not cut at center. 1.8 degrees is the MR-1 chart's helical-ramp figure and is used for the metals. Softer materials ramp steeper so the entry move stays short.",
  "_rules": "Invariants every entry holds, checked by tools/check_materials.mjs: plunge is 30-40% of feed; stepdown stays under half the tool diameter; feed <= 2540 mm/min and spindle <= 8000 rpm; stepover in (0, 0.5]; feed never falls while the spindle holds steady.",
  "_source": "https://assets.langmuirsystems.com/file/CuttingParameters-GettingStartedReferenceGuide-Rev11_30_2022.pdf",
  "default": "aluminum_6061",
